    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25687" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lāĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lajus</span></b> , i (voc. Lai,
			<i><span class="en">Stat. Th.
			7, 355</span></i>), m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λάιος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>son of Labdacus, king of Thebes, and father of
			Œdipus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 4, 33, 71</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fat. 13,
				30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 2, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">66</span></i>.
			—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lāĭădes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <i>a male descendant
				of Laius</i>, i. e. <i>Œdipus</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. M.
				7, 759</span></i>.</div>
